dd up the products of corresponding components:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n(2\\mathbf{u}) \\cdot \\mathbf{v} &= 2 \\cdot 2 + (-2) \\cdot (-5) + 2 \\cdot 1 +  4 \\cdot 0 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&= 4+10+2+0 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&= 16\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":1849,"name":"Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space"},"example":{"id":4784,"title":"Calculating the Dot Product of Two Vectors"},"group":{"id":12469,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241015,"answer":{"id":62264539,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:59:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12843},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264560,"created":"2026-10-15T12:59:40.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13621,"number":12,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:59 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":73939,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":4784,"text":"<p>Let $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{bmatrix} 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{bmatrix} 5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix}.$ What is $\\left(\\dfrac 1 2\\mathbf{a}\\right) \\cdot \\mathbf{b}?$</p>\n","choice1":"$24$","choice2":"$12$","choice3":"$48$","choice4":"$18$","choice5":"$36$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, multiplying each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by $\\dfrac 1 2$, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac 1 2 \\mathbf{a} &= \\dfrac 1 2 \\begin{bmatrix} 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10 \\end{bmatrix} \n= \\begin{bmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\end{bmatrix}\\!.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\left(\\dfrac 1 2\\mathbf{a}\\right) \\cdot \\mathbf{b} &= 2 \\cdot 5 + (-1) \\cdot (-3) + 1 \\cdot 1 +  3 \\cdot 0 + 5\\cdot 2 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&= 10+3+1+0+10 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&= 24\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":1849,"name":"Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space"},"example":{"id":4784,"title":"Calculating the Dot Product of Two Vectors"},"group":{"id":12469,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241015,"answer":{"id":62264560,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:59:40.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13621},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264589,"created":"2026-10-15T12:59:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12053,"number":13,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:59 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":73938,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4784,"text":"<p>If $\\mathbf{r} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{s} = \\begin{bmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{bmatrix}$, then $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\mathbf{s} =$</p>\n","choice1":"$11$","choice2":"$15$","choice3":"$19$","choice4":"$7$","choice5":"$16$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\mathbf{s} &= r_1 \\cdot s_1 + r_2 \\cdot s_2 + r_3 \\cdot s_3 + r_4 \\cdot s_4 + r_5\\cdot s_5\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&= 1 \\cdot 3 + (-1) \\cdot (-4) + 3 \\cdot 1 + 5 \\cdot 1 + 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&= 3 + 4 + 3 + 5 - 4 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&= 11\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":1849,"name":"Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space"},"example":{"id":4784,"title":"Calculating the Dot Product of Two Vectors"},"group":{"id":12469,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241015,"answer":{"id":62264589,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:59:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12053},"graphic":false