m the equation $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\mathbf{s}=7,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\mathbf{s} &= 7 \\\\[3pt]\n(x-2) \\cdot 1  + 2 \\cdot 3 + (-3) \\cdot x + 1 \\cdot (-2) + 1\\cdot 1&= 7 \\\\[3pt]\nx - 2 + 6 - 3x - 2 + 1 &= 7 \\\\[3pt]\n-2x+3 &= 7 \\\\[3pt]\n2x &= -4 \\\\[3pt]\nx &= -2\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Therefore, we conclude that $x=-2.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1849,"name":"Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space"},"example":{"id":4785,"title":"Finding the Value of an Unknown Quantity in an Expression Involving the Dot Product"},"group":{"id":12470,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241015,"answer":{"id":62264716,"cread":"2026-10-15T13:00:56.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15997},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264735,"created":"2026-10-15T13:01:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15026,"number":17,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 1:01 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":105111,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":4785,"text":"<p>Let\n$\\mathbf{r}=\\begin{bmatrix} -3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ z \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{s}=\\begin{bmatrix} 2 \\\\ z+1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ z \\\\ 7 \\end{bmatrix}.$\nIf $\\mathbf{r}\\cdot \\mathbf{s}=1$, find the value of $z.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-6$","choice2":"$-7$","choice3":"$8$","choice4":"$0$","choice5":"$6$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Starting from the equation $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\mathbf{s}=1,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $z$ and then solve for $z$ in the resulting equation:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\mathbf{s} &= 1 \\\\[3pt]\n(-3) \\cdot 2  + 6 \\cdot (z+1) + z \\cdot (-9) + 4 \\cdot z + 1\\cdot 7&= 1 \\\\[3pt]\n-6 + 6z + 6 - 9z + 4z + 7 &= 1 \\\\[3pt]\nz &= -6\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Therefore, we conclude that $z=-6.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1849,"name":"Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space"},"example":{"id":4785,"title":"Finding the Value of an Unknown Quantity in an Expression Involving the Dot Product"},"group":{"id":12470,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241015,"answer":{"id":62264735,"cread":"2026-10-15T13:01:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15026},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264779,"created":"2026-10-15T13:01:36.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":16930,"number":18,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 1:01 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:17","question":{"id":73944,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":4785,"text":"<p>Let\n$\\mathbf{v}=\\begin{bmatrix} -2 \\\\ p \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{w}=\\begin{bmatrix} 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ p \\end{bmatrix}.$\nIf $\\mathbf{v}\\cdot \\mathbf{w}=3$, find the value of $p.$</p>\n","choice1":"$2$","choice2":"$3$","choice3":"$1$","choice4":"$4$","choice5":"$7$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Starting from the equation $\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}=3,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $p$ and then solve for $p$ in the resulting equation:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w} &= 3 \\\\[3pt]\n-2 \\cdot 2  + p \\cdot (-4) + 5 \\cdot 3 + (-2) \\cdot (-3) + (-3)\\cdot p&= 3 \\\\[3pt]\n-4 - 4p + 15 + 6 - 3p &= 3 \\\\[3pt]\n-7p + 17 &= 3 \\\\[3pt]\n7p &= 14 \\\\[3pt]\np &= 2\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Therefore, we conclude that $p=2.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1849,"name":"Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space"},"example":{"id":4785,"title":"Finding the Value of an Unknown Quantity in an Expression Involving the Dot Product"},"group":{"id":12470,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241015,"answer":{"id":62264779,"cread":"2026-10-15T13:01:36.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":16930},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264799,"created":"2026-10-15T13:01:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":16710,"number":19,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 1:01 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:17","question":{"id":73947,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":4785,"text":"<p>Let $\\mathbf{r} = \\begin{bmatrix} 3 \\\\ \\dfrac{2}{x^2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ x \\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{s} = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ x^4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -1 \\end{bmatrix}.$\nIf $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\mathbf{s} = 0$ and $x &lt;    0$, find the value of $x.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-1$","choice2":"$-\\dfrac 2 3$","choice3":"$-2$","choice4":"$-\\dfrac 3 2$","choice5":"$-3$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Starting from the equation $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\mathbf{s}=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\mathbf{s} &= 0 \\\\[5pt]\n3\\cdot (-1)+\\dfrac{2}{x^2} \\cdot x^4 + 0 \\cdot 8 + x \\cdot (-1) &= 0 \\\\[5pt]\n-3+ 2x^2 + 0 - x &= 0\\\\[5pt]\n2x^2 - x - 3 &= 0 \\\\[5pt]\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Now, using the quadratic formula, we obtain</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\nx &= \\dfrac{-(-1) \\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^2-4(2)(-3)}}{2(2)} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{25}}{4} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{1 \\pm 5}{4}.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>So, we get two solutions, $x_1=\\dfrac 3 2$ and $x_2=-1.$ Since we need $x &lt;    0$, our final answer is $x=-1$ only.</p>\n","topic":{"id":1849,"name":"Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space"},"example":{"id":4785,"title":"Finding the Value of an Unknown Quantity in an Expression Involving the Dot Product"},"group":{"id":12470,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241015,"answer":{"id":62264799,"cread":"2026-10-15T13:01:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":16710},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62264855,"created":"2026-10-15T13:02:18.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":16670,"number":20,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 1:02 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:17","question":{"id":35098,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":4785,"text":"<p>Let $\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1\\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{bmatrix} k \\\\ 4 \\\\-5 \\\\ k+2 \\end{bmatrix}.$ If $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=0$, find the value of $k.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-2$","choice2":"$-4$","choice3":"$0$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{16}{7}$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{24}{7}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Starting from the equation $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $k$ and then solve for $k$ in the resulting equation:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} &= 0 \\\\[3pt]\n1\\cdot k + 3\\cdot 4 + 2\\cdot (-5) + 6\\cdot (k+2) &= 0 \\\\[3pt]\nk +12 -10 + 6k+12 &= 0 \\\\[3pt]\n7k+14 &= 0 \\\\[3pt]\n7k &= -14 \\\\[3pt]\nk &= -2\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Therefore, we conclude that $k=-2.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1849,"name":"Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space"},"example":{"id":4785,"title":"Finding the Value of an Unknown Quantity in an Expression Involving the Dot Product"},"group":{"id":12470,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14241015,"answer":{"id":62264855,"cread":"2026-10-15T13:02:18.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":16670},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultyS